From 5a7ef49f491d52e46d533613231b14a25ed3fc56 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Destrudos6 <3411622425@qq.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 12:45:02 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] Add a cached-subtitles browser to the bisub settings

Every finished translation now writes a .meta sidecar next to its
cache file, recording the video title and id, source and target
language, model, cue count and timestamp (failures are logged and
never fail the translation itself).

The new "Cached subtitles" entry in the bisub settings lists the
completed bilingual subtitle files, newest first, with title,
language, model, line count and date. Entries from before the sidecar
existed fall back to the file name and a cue count scanned from the
file. Tapping an entry shows the full WebVTT text in a scrollable,
text-selectable viewer, and a neutral button deletes the cache entry
(after confirmation) so the video is translated again on demand.
